# Own-wording Tome of Heroes magic items, chunk C (Old Elvish Rose to Wolfsbane).
ITEMS = []; SP = {}; WPN = {}; GEAR = []
MASTERY = {}
WDESC = {}

def add(name, typ, rar, att, text, **o):
    ITEMS.append((name, typ, rar, att, text, o))

_W = "Worts are the magical herbs of Tome of Heroes. Each plant has a Minor Wort anyone can use, a Ceremony Wort that needs a ritual and a number of cuttings, and a Cultivated Wort that appears in a garden grown for the stated time. "
_HG = "A heartglow lantern is a hexagonal crystal in a metal frame that burns no fuel, so it suits caverns where air is scarce. While holding it, use an action to make it shed bright light in a 20-foot radius and dim light for 20 feet more. The light lasts until you use a bonus action to repeat the command word, or until no living creature holds or carries it. Each lantern gains an extra effect when infused with vitality. A creature touching it can use an action to infuse it, lowering that creature's hit point maximum by its Proficiency Bonus until it finishes a rest, and the lantern gains charges equal to that amount. A lantern can hold any number of charges from any number of creatures, but each creature can infuse a given lantern only once between long rests. "

add("Old Elvish Rose", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 0, _W + "Themes: contradictions, grace, peaceful intentions. Found near fey homes, where proposals were made, and around forgotten towers. A flowering shrub with alternate leaves, stems covered in sickle-shaped thorns, and broad cup-like flowers in white, pink, yellow and red. **Minor Wort.** As an action, cut a rose across the blade of a weapon that deals Slashing damage to make thorns sprout from it for 1 minute. While thorny, the weapon deals an extra 1d6 Piercing damage to any target it hits. **Ceremony Wort (2nd level).** Spend 10 minutes drawing a bath infused with roses. A creature that soaks in it for 1 hour, which can be during a rest, has Advantage on saves against Charmed and Frightened until it finishes a rest. If it already had Advantage against one of them when it leaves the bath, it is immune to that condition instead. Needs 2 cuttings. **Cultivated Wort (9th level).** A garden grown for at least 26 weeks quells strong emotion. A hostile humanoid or beast that enters or starts its turn in or within 100 feet of the garden makes a Charisma save or becomes indifferent toward creatures it was hostile to. This ends if it is attacked or harmed, or sees an ally harmed. Any effect making a humanoid or beast Charmed or Frightened is suppressed while it is inside the garden, and resumes when it leaves if the duration has not run out. Otherwise it works like calm emotions.")
add("Paired Gauntlets of Striking", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 1, "Leather gloves reinforced with steel plates and decorated with two humanoids fighting side by side. While you and another creature each wear one of the gauntlets and are both within 5 feet of the same creature, you both have Advantage on the first attack roll you make against that creature on each of your turns.")
add("Phase Arrow", "Weapon", "Uncommon", 0, "Any arrow. When you make a ranged attack with this arrow, the attack ignores cover, because the arrow dips briefly into the Shadowfell on its way. If the target has total cover and you know which space it is in, you can fire the arrow at it with Disadvantage on the attack roll.")
add("Potion Belt", "Wondrous Item", "Common", 0, "A plain brown leather belt with a band of flexible pale blue crystal. As an action, pour a potion onto the band, which absorbs it and turns deep blue. The band holds only one potion. This belt has a single band. While wearing it, use an action to speak its command word and gain the potion's benefits as if you had drunk it.")
add("Potion of Infinite Possibilities", "Potion", "Very Rare", 0, "A deep purple potion swirling with glittering flashes of red, green and blue, smelling faintly of ozone. For 1 hour after drinking it, you have Blindsight out to 60 feet. When you roll a 1 on an ability check, saving throw or attack roll, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll. You can see into the Ethereal Plane, where ethereal creatures and objects look ghostly and translucent. When it ends, you are Stunned until the end of your next turn as your mind reels from losing the mind-altering effects.")
add("Pouch of Runestones", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0, "An ordinary-looking hide bag that seems empty, but reaching in finds flat bone tiles. It weighs 1/2 pound. As an action, pull a tile and throw it up in front of you. It floats 5 feet off the ground and shows a rune. Make a DC 12 Wisdom check. On a success the rune is upright, on a failure it is reversed. Roll a d12 on the upright or reversed table. Any save the rune calls for uses DC 15. The tile vanishes after showing its rune, but the bag never runs out. After use, do not use the bag again until the next dawn. Each further use before then raises the Wisdom check DC by 5 for each tile drawn after the first. You can be under several runes at once. Unless noted, a rune lasts until you finish a rest. **Upright runes.** 1 Ansuz (Truth): zone of truth centered on you and moving with you for 1 hour. 2 Naudiz (Necessity): Advantage on your next saving throw. 3 Hagalaz (Winter): you can cast ice storm once. 4 Laukaz (Sea): you breathe air and water for 5 hours. 5 Algiz (Protection): +2 bonus to AC. 6 Mannaz (Teamwork): you and up to five creatures you can see gain 10 temporary hit points. 7 Isaz (Ice): your hits deal an extra 1d6 Cold damage. 8 Berkanan (Bear Maiden): as an action, cast polymorph on yourself to become a brown bear, keeping your Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma, and end it early as a bonus action. 9 Perto (Mystery): cast disguise self at will. 10 Ehwaz (Freedom): spend 5 feet of movement to escape nonmagical restraints such as manacles or a grapple automatically. 11 Raido (Easy Travel): Speed +10 feet. 12 Kaunen (Enlightenment): cast lesser restoration once as a bonus action. **Reversed runes.** 1 Ansuz (Falsehood): you believe everything you hear is a lie. 2 Naudiz (Consequence): Disadvantage on your next saving throw. 3 Hagalaz (Blizzard): Otiluke's freezing sphere triggers centered on you. 4 Laukaz (Sky): reverse gravity triggers centered on you, ending at the start of your next turn. 5 Algiz (Vulnerability): AC reduced by 2. 6 Mannaz (Dissension): you and friendly creatures within 30 feet have Disadvantage on attack rolls while within 10 feet of each other. 7 Isaz (Ice): Vulnerability to Cold damage. 8 Berkanan (Bear Matron): a brown bear appears in the nearest free space and attacks you. 9 Perto (Unwanted Revelation): Disadvantage on Charisma checks. 10 Ehwaz (Shackles): maze targets you, lasting 10 minutes or until you escape. 11 Raido (Hard Travel): Speed reduced by 10 feet. 12 Kaunen (Insanity): you suffer a long-term madness.")
add("Serpentine Sandals", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 1, "Glistening snake-skin sandals. While wearing them, you ignore difficult terrain from marsh, swamp or other shallow water, such as a rain-soaked rooftop. You also have Advantage on ability checks and saves to escape a grapple or the Restrained condition.")
add("Shattershot Arrow", "Weapon", "Uncommon", 0, "Any arrow. When you hit a creature with it, the target takes an extra 3d6 Thunder damage as the arrow gives a sudden loud ring. Each creature made of inorganic material such as stone, crystal or metal within 10 feet of the target makes a DC 13 Constitution save, taking 3d6 Thunder damage on a failure or half on a success. A nonmagical object that nobody wears or carries within 10 feet of the target also takes the damage.")
add("Soulbound Wraps", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 1, "Cloth hand wraps embroidered with symbols of balance and meditation. When you hit a creature with an unarmed strike while wearing them, you can reduce the damage you deal by up to 10, drawing some of the energy back into you. You regain 1 ki point for every 10 damage you choose not to deal. Once you have regained ki points equal to half your Proficiency Bonus this way, the wraps unravel and cannot be worn again until the next dawn. Requires attunement by a monk.", by="Monk")
add("Stasis Stone", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0, "A small purple crystalline stone, 3/4 inch across, weighing an ounce. Usually 1d4 + 2 are found together. As an action, throw one up to 30 feet. It explodes on impact and is destroyed. Each creature within 10 feet of where it landed makes a DC 15 Constitution save or is Petrified until the end of its next turn as the stone releases temporal magic and freezes it in time.")
add("Tumblesafe Heartglow Lantern", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0, _HG + "**Tumblesafe.** If you or a friendly creature you can see within 40 feet falls while you hold or carry this lantern, use a Reaction and spend 1 or more charges to slow the fall. Each charge beyond the first extends the lantern's light by 5 feet. Each falling creature and object in the lantern's light descends 60 feet per round and takes no falling damage, and keeps descending at that rate until it lands, even if it leaves the light.")
add("Victory Banner", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 1, "A small banner on a short haft that can be fixed to a backpack, saddle or similar gear. It has 3 charges and regains all spent charges at dawn. Spend 1 charge to give yourself Advantage on weapon attacks for 1 minute. When you roll a 20 on a weapon attack, you can spend 1 charge to move up to your Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks. You must be within 5 feet of the banner to spend its charges.", ch=[3, "3", "dawn"])
add("Wolfsbane", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 0, _W + "Themes: lycanthropy, transformation, the moon. Found in secluded groves, near the borders of the Material Plane and Shadowfell, and where creatures or objects were forced to change shape. A poisonous flowering plant with dark green palm-like leaves on tall stems, each crowned with a cluster of hooded flowers in blue, purple, white, yellow or pink. **Minor Wort.** As an action, crush and sprinkle petals over a creature or object that was turned to stone or forced to change shape, such as by polymorph. It reverts to its true form at once. An unwilling creature can make a Charisma save to be unaffected. **Ceremony Wort (7th level).** Soak petals in a bowl of shallow water under the full moon for 10 minutes to imbue them with the moon's power. You and up to 5 other creatures can eat them to cast polymorph on yourselves, each becoming a dire wolf and keeping Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma. The change lasts until dawn's first light touches a transformed creature, it drops to 0 hit points or dies, or it is forced back by other means. Needs 3 cuttings. **Cultivated Wort (5th level).** A garden grown for at least 8 weeks cleanses lycanthropy. An afflicted creature that rests in it is cured, but must make death saving throws during the rest as the garden's magic attacks the affliction. If it fails three before succeeding on three, it dies, though the lycanthropy is removed. If the lycanthropy is hereditary, such as a werewolf with a werewolf parent, the garden removes it only if the creature is willing and stays a week, and makes the death saves only on its first rest there.")

add("Axe of Many Strikes", "Weapon", "Uncommon", 1, "Any axe. You have a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with this magic weapon. When you hit a creature with it, you can choose to deal no damage and instead store the attack's energy in the blade for 1 minute. It can store up to three attacks. When you hit a creature with it while at least one attack is stored, you can release one or more stored attacks, adding their damage to the current attack. Each time you release stored attacks, there is a 10 percent chance the axe explodes, dealing 2d6 Force damage to you for each attack released and destroying the axe.", fx={"atk": 1, "dmg": 1}, base=["Battleaxe", "Handaxe", "Greataxe"])
add("Momentblade", "Weapon", "Rare", 1, "Any axe or sword. You have a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with this magic weapon. When you roll a 20 on an attack roll with it, the target vanishes and shuffles forward in time. At the end of your next turn it returns to the space it left, or the nearest free space, unaware that any time has passed. If the target is concentrating on a spell and succeeds on the check to keep Concentration after taking damage from your attack, the round it was gone does not count against the spell's remaining duration.", fx={"atk": 1, "dmg": 1}, base=["Longsword", "Battleaxe", "Greatsword", "Shortsword"])
add("Stormheart Bow", "Weapon", "Rare", 1, "Any bow, made from dragon bone and fey heartstring. When you hit with an attack using it, the target takes an extra 1d6 Lightning damage. It has 5 charges and regains 1d4 + 1 spent charges at dawn. **Iceshard Arrow.** When you hit, spend 3 charges to turn the arrow to ice and shatter it in mid-air. Choose up to three targets within 30 feet of your original target. The original target takes normal damage, and each chosen target takes 1d6 Cold damage. **Thunder Arrow.** When you hit, spend 2 charges to release a peal of thunder. The target takes normal damage, and each creature within 15 feet of it makes a DC 15 Constitution save, taking 2d6 Thunder damage on a failure or half on a success.", base=["Longbow", "Shortbow"], ch=[5, "1d4+1", "dawn"], xd=["Hit: +1d6 Lightning"])
